WEBVTT

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:01.345
in some cases, like an hour,

00:20:01.369 --> 00:20:04.263
and I don't know about you,
but when I talk to somebody else,

00:20:04.287 --> 00:20:07.446
I'm very rarely staring at their face
for all 60 minutes.

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:10.073
AG: There's a fun study
that tracked people's reactions

00:20:10.097 --> 00:20:12.516
to seeing a large virtual
face on their screen.

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:15.617
The most common response was to flinch.

00:20:15.641 --> 00:20:17.206
(Music)

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:20.806
AG: We know face-to-face interaction
is critical for establishing trust,

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:22.702
for building that shared understanding

00:20:22.726 --> 00:20:24.916
that Martine Haas has
found is so important.

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:26.386
But once trust exists,

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:28.220
I think we should all have the license

00:20:28.244 --> 00:20:30.656
to turn off our video feeds
from time to time.